## Verification

Read-only audit only. I did **not edit files**.

The current `config/settings.yaml` differs from `config/settings.yaml.bak_pre_resolver_stripdown_030145` by exactly **9 scalar/list paths**:

| Edit | Verified |
|---|---:|
| `regime_fade.enabled: true -> false` | yes |
| `direction.enforce: true -> false` | yes |
| `eth_macro.eth_momentum_confirm.buy_yes: ['5m','15m','1h'] -> []` | yes |
| `eth_macro.eth_momentum_confirm.buy_no: ['5m','15m','1h'] -> []` | yes |
| `sol_macro.buy_no_tape_map_veto_up: true -> false` | yes |
| `hype_macro.buy_no_tape_map_veto_up: true -> false` | yes |
| `xrp_macro.buy_no_tape_map_veto_up: true -> false` | yes |
| `doge_macro.buy_no_tape_map_veto_up: true -> false` | yes |
| `bnb_macro.buy_no_tape_map_veto_up: true -> false` | yes |

The July 20 `+869` config has **no top-level `direction:` block**, so it uses the default quant/native side path. Current `direction.enforce:false` is behaviorally equivalent for side override: the override module returns the quant side unchanged unless `enforce` is true. See [direction_override.py](/Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main%201/src/analysis/direction_override.py:133) and [sol_macro.py](/Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main%201/src/strategies/sol_macro.py:1484).

## Answers

**A. `direction.enforce:false` looks safe relative to the +869 native-side behavior.**  
It does not enable a new resolver; it disables the Claude-written override from driving side. With `mode: claude` and `enforce:false`, mismatches are logged but `quant_side` is returned unchanged. `override_when_quant_neutral:true` also does **not** matter while `enforce:false`, because `applied = enforce and differs`.

Skeptical note: native side is not proven “good” in isolation. The shadow `side_resolver_v2` doc says current champion/native-heavy selection was around coinflip, with ETH worse. That is an alpha-quality concern, not a safety bug that Claude override was clearly correcting. I found no code evidence that native has a known polarity inversion that requires Claude override.

**B. Remaining blunt side/global gates still present:**  
The strip removed the four named stacks, but not all side constraints. Current still has lane-level and strategy-level gates, including `lane_management.execution_enforcement_enabled:true`, per-lane `disable_*`, `enforce_alt_1h_alignment:true` on SOL/HYPE/XRP/DOGE/BNB, RSI hard gates, oracle requirements, late-window blocks, and `tape_veto_60s_enabled:true` on several lanes.

The important nuance: top-level `regime_fade.enabled:false` disables the **post-signal rolling-WR suppressor** in `main.py`, but the older per-strategy `fade_regime` side inversion remains possible when `fade_regime_windows` is non-empty. In current config, XRP keeps `['5m','1h']` and DOGE keeps `['5m','15m']`, matching the intentional “do not blindly revert disables” posture. See [sol_macro.py](/Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main%201/src/strategies/sol_macro.py:1520).

**C. Over-strip risk:**  
Moderate, not catastrophic.

Highest-risk removal is **`direction.enforce:false`**, because if Claude was actively writing `FLAT` or opposite-side overrides, those are now observe-only and native resumes trading. But this matches the +869 behavior.

Second risk is **ETH momentum confirm off**. The code comment says default-on momentum guards were historically breakeven-to-harmful, but the current config comments claim recent ETH bleed evidence. So this is a deliberate re-baseline, not obviously safe. Watch ETH first.

Third risk is **BUY_NO tape-map veto off** across five alts. This can reopen shorts into UP tape. However, `require_tape_direction` was already false, many lane disables remain, 60s tape veto may still block some bad entries, and lane management is still enforced.

I do **not** see an obvious firehose path from these 9 edits alone because sizing/risk/lane management/entry windows/oracle/liquidity/edge gates remain.

**D. Post-restart Smoke Watch**

Track the first **20-30 closed trades** and the first **2-4 hours** separately.

Break conditions I’d use:

| Signal | Break Condition |
|---|---|
| Frequency | Trades/hour > **2x** the last comparable dry-run session, or > **12 trades/hour** sustained for 2 hours |
| Direction override | `DIRECTION_OVERRIDE ... applied=True` appears at all with `enforce=false` |
| Native-side quality | `side_source_counts` dominated by `*_native` and closed WR stays `<42%` after 15+ closes |
| ETH | ETH native sides produce `<40% WR` or net `< -$25` over first 10 ETH closes |
| Tape-veto removal | `BUY_NO` entries with tape `UP` cluster and lose 3+ in a row, especially XRP/ETH/HYPE 15m |
| Regime fade removal | `regime_fade_mid_band_chop` should drop to zero; if mid-confidence reopened trades lose `<40% WR` after 15 closes, rollback candidate |
| Firehose | Open positions stack same-side/same-expiry despite risk checks, or lane management skipped signals unexpectedly stop appearing |

Most useful smoke surfaces: `OPS_JSON last_signal_counts`, strategy `SCAN_DIAG side_source_counts`, `top_skip_reasons`, closed-trade WR by `strategy|window|side|side_source`, and any `DIRECTION_OVERRIDE` log lines.

## Metadata/Summary

